      <article class="card"><div class="tag">07</div><h3>Security Monitoring</h3><p>Monitoring setup, tuned alerts, monthly reporting and agreed escalation during Australian business hours.</p></article>
      <article class="card"><div class="tag">08</div><h3>Policies and Compliance Support</h3><p>Security policies, incident response planning and gap analysis against SMB1001 or ISO 27001.</p></article>
      <article class="card"><div class="tag">AI</div><h3>Secure AI deployment</h3><p>Review access, permissions, logging, data flows and human approval points when new AI workflows are introduced.</p></article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- HOW IT WORKS -->
<section id="how-it-works">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head">
      <div class="eyebrow">How Sharktech delivers</div>
      <h2>Scope the bottleneck first. Build the right solution second.</h2>
      <p>AccrualOS is the fixed-price product layer. Custom service work is scoped separately and quoted per job.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="process">
      <div class="step"><div class="tag">01</div><div><b>Discovery and scope</b><p>Understand what the practice runs, what the business is being asked to prove and which systems are in scope.</p></div></div>
      <div class="step"><div class="tag">02</div><div><b>Permission and access</b><p>Agree what can be reviewed or tested, when the work will occur and who owns approvals.</p></div></div>
      <div class="step"><div class="tag">03</div><div><b>Assessment or build</b><p>Run the agreed security review, hardening, testing or secure AI implementation work.</p></div></div>
      <div class="step"><div class="tag">04</div><div><b>Findings and priorities</b><p>Provide clear management findings plus technical detail for the people implementing fixes.</p></div></div>
      <div class="step"><div class="tag">05</div><div><b>Fix, retest and support</b><p>Help close agreed findings, confirm fixes where applicable and define any ongoing support separately.</p></div></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

